# Docker build context excludes. The Dockerfile copies named files/dirs
# into each stage rather than doing a broad COPY, so this list exists to
# keep the build context itself small and secret-free — not as the only
# line of defense against secrets entering an image layer.

.git
.github
node_modules
.next
out
dist-customer-auth
dist-workforce-auth
dist-customer-commerce
dist-operations
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report

# env files — everything except the committed, secret-free templates.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test
!.env.docker.example

# Explicit belt-and-suspenders: these generated/ignored files must never
# reach the build context even if a future .env.* pattern above is loosened.
.env.local
.env.docker.local
.env.runtime.docker.local
.env.migration.docker.local
.env.verify.docker.local
.env.customer-auth.docker.local
.env.workforce-auth.docker.local
.env.customer-commerce.docker.local
.env.operations.docker.local

# figma-sync reference screenshots — large, not needed for the app image.
figma-sync/*.png
*.log

# IDE / OS metadata
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker itself
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml

# Non-repo reference/wireframe assets and root-level design images — not
# used by the build, no reason to ship them into the build context. Anchored
# to the context root (leading "/") so this does NOT also match the real
# application assets under public/assets/**.
Boba Bear Landing Page Wireframe Updated
Boba_Bear_Design_System_Updated
test-results*
playwright-report*
scripts/assortment/configure-outlet-operating-uat.ts
/*.png
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
Updated_BOBA BEAR_ DESIGN SYSTEM (V1.1).md
boba-bear-design-system.md
